" "q-85069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "34"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-1\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 2| \\\\  & =|5-8| \\\\  & =|-3| \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|8\\cdot 2-7\\cdot (-3)| \\\\  & =|16-(-21)| \\\\  & =37.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "37"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-84701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-84701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|9\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 7| \\\\  & =|0-35| \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-84701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988"} {"question" "q-84701" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-84701" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-84701" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "35"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-12281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/d9e210f0bfd9ada2dd147068fe0cf06fa85ad049f79bb7e844931b6037867f97.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-12281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=2\\cdot 4=8.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=5\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 3=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-12281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988"} {"question" "q-12281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-12281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "24"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "52"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-12281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-9302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/4f31b9f180b1b766451685428fc289766832fe5d0c7d8902a601ebf060eab0e7.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-9302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 0=-10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-10|\\cdot 4\\pi  \\\\  & =40\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-9302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988"} {"question" "q-9302" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-9302" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\pi "] ["math" "160"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "40\\pi "] ["math" "80\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a