(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 5=15.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-316607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988"} {"question" "q-316607" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "q-316607" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "60"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "b6c8cd7f29652ab1b72a7678983e9fabd844459040fd190b544a5d8e176daeed"} {"question" "e-7454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/example-7454.json" "file_sha256" "33ce61ff3b3eff90b73d97587fc8ed27370ec5f6d5a6c71547fc1706adcf4d0f"} {"question" "e-7454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|\\det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|8-3| \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/example-7454.json" "file_sha256" "33ce61ff3b3eff90b73d97587fc8ed27370ec5f6d5a6c71547fc1706adcf4d0f"} {"question" "e-5470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/e8ff769df4089e6ed9a47d56d7317acf41b8aef6a255abc705c0e7ec31a446ea.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/example-5470.json" "file_sha256" "55ecf32c17cf99589905144705fe9dce1cb4f7ade6f9028449f898c99cdaf701"} {"question" "e-5470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 -  2 \\cdot (-1) = 10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/example-5470.json" "file_sha256" "55ecf32c17cf99589905144705fe9dce1cb4f7ade6f9028449f898c99cdaf701"} {"question" "e-5471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5),$ and $(-2,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/example-5471.json" "file_sha256" "d6416d61a42f3975e658121ad2003cdbe839dfbeac627df82ef9a5b765acd2e3"} {"question" "e-5471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/ee8f0cf16983d87fa505303ed6372a3f389518d05b3e13f2e9e2121038792b84.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 -  5 \\cdot (-2) = -11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-11|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/example-5471.json" "file_sha256" "d6416d61a42f3975e658121ad2003cdbe839dfbeac627df82ef9a5b765acd2e3"}] "usage" {"e-5470" [] "e-5471" [] "q-9302" [] "e-7454" []} "basis" 1044 "retractions" [[17592186092848 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/989/Source/Images/q-9302.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186092074 :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186092074 :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $\\mid \\det(T) \\mid$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & &= & 2 \\cdot 4 - 3 \\cdot 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\mid 8 - 3 \\mid \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186092019 :question/problem "Consider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/989/Source/Images/db07fd70ec06ccd7ac9258c2f4c75f22.png)"] [17592186092019 :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = \\mid \\det(T) \\mid \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T$, we get\n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot (-1) = 10\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nArea(T(D)) &= \\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & \\cdot Area(D) \\\\ = & 10\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 60\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186092020 :question/problem "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5)$, and $(-2,1)$. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186092020 :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/989/Source/Images/6c06e31f3407ba3e54c61c5b222b6d9d.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = \\mid \\det(T) \\mid \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T$, we get\n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 - 5 \\cdot (-2) = -11\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nArea(T(D)) &= \\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & \\cdot Area(D) \\\\ = & -11\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 66\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186091554 17592186091555 17592186091556 17592186091557 17592186091558] "immutable_fields" [[17592186091553 :answer-field/correct] [17592186091553 :answer-field/id] [17592186091553 :answer-field/key] [17592186091553 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
